Object.assign(n[7890],{"id":"potato-picker","lane":"windows-privesc","title":"Potato Picker — which SeImpersonate exploit fits this box","hypothesis":"Found SeImpersonatePrivilege on whoami /priv? A potato gets you SYSTEM — but the RIGHT potato depends on the OS build and whether DCOM works. The decision tree: modern Windows (10/11, Server 2012–2022) → GodPotato (DCOM-based, no CLSID hunting); Win10/2019 → PrintSpoofer (named-pipe spoof, very reliable); PrintSpoofer fails or DCOM broken → RoguePotato (needs port 135 reachable); old 7/2008–2012 → JuicyPotato with a valid CLSID list; everything fails → SweetPotato bundles the rest. Manual checks first — the exploit is the last step, not the first.","prereq":n[7891],"produces":n[7893],"commands":n[7894],"expected":n[7898],"onFailure":n[7899],"defender":"SeImpersonate abuse spawns child processes of services as SYSTEM — service binary spawning cmd.exe is the loudest possible alert. Microsoft has been steadily closing potato primitives; assume EDR knows them all.","report":n[7901],"tools":n[7902],"os":n[7903],"refs":n[7904]});
